      "text": "Hey there, how have things been?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 7.83,
      "end": 13.957,
      "text": "Sure. Complementary colors sit opposite each other on the color wheel, like blue and orange or red and green."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 17.267,
      "end": 22.887,
      "text": "Put side by side, they make each other look brighter. Mixed together, they cancel out into a soft gray or brown."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 27.147,
      "end": 32.137,
      "text": "Exactly. A shadow on an orange made with a little blue looks much more alive than plain black."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 39.207,
      "end": 44.127,
      "text": "You can always get it later. Plenty of painters work without black and mix their darks instead."
